From: cormierjohn <49281283+cormierjohn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:42:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: bottom-layer contour compensation for elephant's
 foot

The long bottom exposures flare every edge that touches the build plate: outlines
print wider and holes print smaller. Materials get two settings that move the edges
of the bottom layers before anti-aliasing, in millimetres:

- Bottom outline compensation: negative shrinks outer outlines, positive grows them.
  An island standing inside a hole counts as an outline.
- Bottom hole compensation: negative opens holes, positive closes them.

The two are independent and exact on each axis for non-square pixels. With "Fade
through transition layers" (on by default) the bottom layers get the full amount and
the transition layers a share that steps down with their exposure, reaching none on
the last transition layer, where the exposure is back to normal. Off, the bottom and
transition layers all get the full amount.

Engine (3.4.0): new SliceJobV3 fields bottom_outline_compensation_mm,
bottom_hole_compensation_mm, bottom_compensation_layers and
bottom_compensation_fade_layers, applied in rasterize_layer_rle and
rasterize_layer_with_stats so every raster path gets them (the column-block path
rasterizes compensated layers full width and crops). Contours are classified by
nesting depth and moved with an exact Euclidean distance transform over the layer's
lit bounding box (compensation.rs).

App: a Compensation section in the material editor (its own tab for formats whose
plugin replaces the default material settings), store normalizers, job assembly
(resolveBottomCompensationLayers reads the bottom and transition layer counts the
encoders use), the native bridge, src-tauri and the CLI (new flags; CLI 2.2.0).
Docs: new reference page and updates to the engine, job assembly, CLI and data
storage pages. Also lets LabeledNumberInput accept a minus sign when its minimum is
negative.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
